        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Codes and Standards",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  UPDATE CYCLES:\n    ICC: 3-year update cycle (2018, 2021, 2024 editions)\n    IAPMO: same 3-year cycle\n    States/localities: adopt on variable lag\n    Common situation (2024): many jurisdictions still on 2018 cycle\n    Some: 2015 cycle\n    Bottom line: your jurisdiction may be 1-2 editions behind"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-CODES-STANDARDS.md#011",
      "path": [
        "09-CODES-STANDARDS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:plumbing:09-codes-standards, git-history:plumbing:09-codes-standards]",
        "canonical_path": "plumbing/09-CODES-STANDARDS.md",
        "concepts": "[codes, standards]",
        "current_path": "plumbing/09-CODES-STANDARDS.md",
        "id": "maxim:plumbing:codes-standards",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "plumbing",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[codes, standards]",
        "section": "plumbing",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Codes and Standards",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "STATE-LEVEL ADOPTION:\n    States pass building code legislation → reference specific\n    edition of model code + state amendments\n    California: Title 24 (California Building Standards Code)\n      Uses modified UPC; significant California amendments\n    New York: uses modified IPC\n    Texas: cities choose their own codes; no statewide mandate\n    (Texas is an exception — local control more extreme)\n    Florida: Florida Building Code (FBC) = modified IBC/IRC + Florida amendments"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-CODES-STANDARDS.md#012",
      "path": [
        "09-CODES-STANDARDS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:plumbing:09-codes-standards, git-history:plumbing:09-codes-standards]",
        "canonical_path": "plumbing/09-CODES-STANDARDS.md",
        "concepts": "[codes, standards]",
        "current_path": "plumbing/09-CODES-STANDARDS.md",
        "id": "maxim:plumbing:codes-standards",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "plumbing",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[codes, standards]",
        "section": "plumbing",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Codes and Standards",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "IAPMO (UPC) vs ICC (IPC) DIFFERENCES:\n    Same fundamental plumbing principles\n    Different organization and numbering\n    Some technical differences:\n      Vent pipe sizing: slightly different table values\n      Wet venting rules: different allowable configurations\n      Trap-to-vent distance: slightly different requirements\n    Cannot mix code references: use one or the other for a project"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-CODES-STANDARDS.md#013",
      "path": [
        "09-CODES-STANDARDS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
