        "section": "plumbing",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Codes and Standards",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The sizing methodology is a probabilistic layer (Hunter's fixture-unit method) on top of Darcy-Weisbach hydraulics: SFU values estimate probable simultaneous demand in GPM, which then feeds into Darcy-Weisbach pipe sizing (ΔP = f(L/D)(ρv²/2), ΔP proportional to Q²). The system curve (required head vs. flow) is a parabola; the supply head curve (available pressure minus elevation losses) determines the operating point. See `04-SUPPLY-SYSTEMS.md` for the full Darcy-Weisbach treatment."
    },
